      "message": "Perhaps we should be bumping from 13u to BPFLOADER_T_VERSION (19u) here...\n\nThe real dependency is on v0.18 which added pin_subdir support\n\n(v0.19 enables selinux_context, but prior to that it just gets ignored but things work, since selinux_context just wasn\u0027t available yet)\n\nIt\u0027s the pin_subdir support which changes resulting path which is a requirement, because without it we won\u0027t be able to find things.\n\nConsidering v0.18 and v0.19 landed June 21st and June 23rd, it doesn\u0027t really matter I think.\n\nThe issue is bpfloader \u003c 18 / 19 will:\n\nwithout the change - load the file, and we\u0027ll fail later when we can\u0027t find maps/programs, because pin_subdir was ignored, and pinned into wrong paths\n\nwith the change - ignore the file, and we\u0027ll still fail later... due to missing maps/programs\n\nProbably easier to debug the latter.\n\n---\n\nSo the real question is: by going from 13u to 18u or 19u here...\nWhat do we lose support for?\n\nT beta 2 is at v0.11, so long incompatible.\n\nT beta 4 should already include v0.19 when it is cut in a week or so, so should be good no matter what.\n\nT beta 3 is at 14 - at least on the release branch... but we had issues with netd using the hardcoded paths in p/m/C which weren\u0027t correct.\n\nNot sure what the beta 3.0 / 3.1 / 3.2 real states are...",
